    "# Notebook 01 — Dataset Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "**FraudGuard AI | Phase 3 — Dataset Understanding**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Systematically understand the structure, schema, features, target variable, and class distribution of each approved dataset. This notebook does NOT perform EDA — it serves as a verified schema reference for all downstream notebooks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Datasets covered:**\n",
    "1. PaySim (PRIMARY)\n",
    "2. ULB Credit Card Fraud (BENCHMARK)\n",
    "3. IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection (SECONDARY)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset roles (from Phase 2):**\n",
    "- **PaySim**: Primary training dataset — clear financial features, realistic imbalance, suitable for explainability\n",
    "- **ULB**: Benchmark only — anonymised PCA features, no explainability possible\n",
    "- **IEEE-CIS**: Secondary/advanced — 394 features, high missingness, complex join required\n",
    "- **UPI Fraud**: REJECTED — unrealistic 17% fraud rate, highly synthetic feature set\n",
    "\n",
    "**Safety rules enforced in this notebook:**\n",
    "- Raw data files are opened read-only\n",
    "- No rows are deleted or modified\n",
    "- No columns are renamed or dropped\n",
    "- No resampling is performed\n",
    "- No train/test split is performed here"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as ticker\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot style\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid', palette='muted')\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({'figure.dpi': 120, 'figure.figsize': (10, 4)})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Paths — all read-only\n",
    "RAW = Path('../data/raw')\n",
    "PAYSIM_PATH = RAW / 'PS_20174392719_1491204439457_log.csv'\n",
    "ULB_PATH    = RAW / 'creditcard.csv'\n",
    "IEEE_TX_PATH = RAW / 'IEEE_CIS archive (3)' / 'train_transaction.csv'\n",
    "IEEE_ID_PATH = RAW / 'IEEE_CIS archive (3)' / 'train_identity.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Paths configured.')\n",
    "for p in [PAYSIM_PATH, ULB_PATH, IEEE_TX_PATH, IEEE_ID_PATH]:\n",
    "    status = '✅' if p.exists() else '❌ MISSING'\n",
    "    print(f'  {status}  {p.name}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. PaySim Dataset (PRIMARY)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Source:** E.A. Lopez-Rojas, A. Elmir, S. Axelsson. "PaySim: A financial mobile money simulator for fraud detection." EMSS 2016.  \n",
    "**License:** Open Database License (ODbL)  \n",
    "**Status:** Synthetic — simulated from real M-Pesa transaction logs  \n",
    "**Dataset scope:** Mobile money transactions (cash-in, cash-out, transfer, payment, debit)  \n",
    "**Time coverage:** 30 days (744 steps × 1 hour/step)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why PRIMARY?\n",
    "- Clear, named financial features → suitable for SHAP explainability\n",
    "- Realistic extreme class imbalance (~0.13% fraud)\n",
    "- 6.3M rows → robust cross-validation splits\n",
    "- Well-documented provenance and simulation methodology"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load PaySim — read in chunks to be memory-aware, then concatenate a sample\n",
    "# for schema inspection. Full dataset is used for training.\n",
    "print('Loading PaySim dataset...')\n",
    "df_ps = pd.read_csv(PAYSIM_PATH, low_memory=False)\n",
    "print(f'Shape: {df_ps.shape[0]:,} rows × {df_ps.shape[1]} columns')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
