    "---\n",
    "## 4. Dataset Role Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset | Role | Records | Fraud % | Explainability | Priority |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| PaySim | PRIMARY | 6,362,620 | 0.13% | ✅ Full | 1st |\n",
    "| ULB Credit Card | BENCHMARK | 284,807 | 0.17% | ❌ Anonymised | 2nd |\n",
    "| IEEE-CIS | SECONDARY | 590,540 | 3.50% | ⚠️ Partial | 3rd |\n",
    "| UPI Fraud | REJECTED | 26,393 | 17.22% | N/A | — |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Decision: Why PaySim is PRIMARY\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Interpretable features** → enables meaningful SHAP explanations (`amount`, `oldbalanceOrg`, `type`)\n",
    "2. **Realistic extreme imbalance** (0.13%) → core research problem aligns perfectly\n",
    "3. **Sufficient size** (6.3M) → allows robust stratified train/test splits without resampling bias\n",
    "4. **Zero missing values** → no imputation uncertainty in baseline models\n",
    "5. **Established in literature** → results comparable to published work\n",
    "6. **Clear fraud mechanism** → fraud is limited to CASH_OUT and TRANSFER, enabling targeted feature engineering"
   ]
